#### \(\Omega\) reconstruction

The \(\Omega\) is more difficult to reconstruct than a \(V^{0}\) or the \(\Xi\) because there are fewer \(\Omega\) baryons produced. The default cuts are the same as those in Table 4.4. The geometry of an \(\Omega\) decay is the same as the geometry of a \(\Xi\) decay so similar cuts are applied. The cut described in Equation 4.4, also works to efficiently reconstruct \(\Omega\) decay vertices. An \(\Omega\) baryon has two decay daughters, a \(\Lambda\) and a \(K^{-}\), so an analogous cut can also be applied:

